  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - JAMAICA: TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE: REHABILITATION OF PRIORITY WASTEWATER FACILITIES, through Government of Jamaica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $150,000 grant funds technical assistance (TA) for Jamaica&apos;s National Water Commission (NWC) for a wastewater facility rehabilitation pilot project. This TA will enable the NWC, a statutory body established through an Act of the Jamaican parliament, to improve its ability to evaluate wastewater treatment facility upgrade needs in order to comply with environmental regulations and to improve wastewater treatment facility performance. This project is one of two projects brought to USTDA in connection with the Caribbean Regional Fund for Wastewater Management (CReW), which is financed and managed by the Inter- American Development Bank (IDB). The second pilot project associated with CReW is in Belize and is a separate activity.</narrative>
  </description>
